      "Rule example: Be the first player to play all your dominoes. Score points based on opponents' remaining tiles. First to reach target score (usually 100 or 150) wins.",
      "Turn-flow example: The player with the highest double (9-9 with double-9 set) starts. If not drawn, all players draw one extra tile until found. The first double played starts the 'spinner' with four arms. Subsequent doubles are played crosswise and are 'spinners' - the next three plays must be on the double, creating a chicken foot. After three tiles are played on a double, the arm can be extended normally. Players unable to play draw from the chicken yard. If still unable to play, they pass.",
